# Mem0 Setup Skill

## When to use
When setting up a self-hosted Mem0 server for multiple AI agents to share memory via user_id.

## Steps
1. Clone the Mem0 repository
2. Create a .env file with required configuration
3. Run docker compose up to start the Mem0 server
4. Run make bootstrap to complete setup
5. Configure agents with the correct MEM0_API_KEY

## Example
```bash
git clone https://github.com/mem0/mem0.git
cd mem0
cp .env.example .env
# Edit .env with your API key and server settings
docker compose up -d
make bootstrap
```

## Notes
- Mem0 uses FastAPI + PostgreSQL (pgvector) for storage
- Authentication is via X-API-Key header
- Memory is separated by user_id for each agent
- To share memory between agents, use the same user_id